    wangshuang "Thoughts are trivial and volatile, like a pile of mud. Everyone can give it a squish and make it into whatever shape they want. The mission, however, is homogeneous to one's being - only when mission loosens its grip can thoughts have a moment of freedom, albeit a fake one."

